---
description: JRebirth boundaries and forbidden shortcuts
alwaysApply: true
---
# JRebirth boundaries

Always prefer the mechanisms that the framework already provides over ad-hoc shortcuts.

The following shortcuts are banned by default:

- no `new Thread` for the normal application flow.
- no `Platform.runLater` used as a design pattern.
- no heavy business logic placed inside a View or a Controller.
- no stateful bindings owned by a View when they belong to the Model.
- no `localFacade().globalFacade()` except in rare, hard integration cases.

Whenever you are in doubt, stop and use the relevant skill.
